calibre
-------

Magnitide works with calibre (https://calibre-ebook.com), by Kovid Goyal and
the calibre contributors, and some of its code is derived from calibre's
(Copyright (C) 2008-2026 Kovid Goyal and others, GPLv3). calibre's code is
licensed under version 3 of the GPL only, so the files derived from it are
too, and Magnitide as a whole can be distributed under GPLv3.

Every file derived from calibre names the calibre file it comes from, its
copyright holder and license, and that it was modified, in its first lines:

    git grep -l -E '^(#|//|--) Derived from calibre'

They are:

- crates/plugins/python/compat/: the compatibility package calibre plugins
  run against. It mirrors calibre 9.15's plugin API, and the modules that
  reuse calibre's code (most of calibre/db, calibre/ebooks/metadata,
  calibre/gui2, calibre/utils, calibre/customize) carry the notice, as does
  resources/default_tweaks.py.
- crates/calibre-compat/: schema/metadata_sqlite.sql (calibre's library
  schema), src/sqlfuncs.rs (title sort) and src/write.rs (custom column
  tables).
- crates/core/src/convert/azw3/: the EPUB to AZW3 converter, ported from
  calibre's KF8 writer (src/calibre/ebooks/mobi/writer8/).

calibre/utils/titlecase.py in the compat package derives from calibre's,
which is by Stuart Colville (after John Gruber's original) with changes by
Kovid Goyal, under the MIT license
(http://www.opensource.org/licenses/mit-license.php).

scripts/vendor-calibre.py can copy calibre's own modules into the repository.
It isn't used; if it ever is, what it copies keeps calibre's license and
notices (it writes LICENSE.calibre and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md beside them).


Other bundled material
----------------------

- crates/plugins/python/compat/resources/images/lucide/: Lucide icons,
  ISC license (LICENSE in that folder).
- crates/plugins/python/compat/resources/localization/iso639.json: language
  names from the iso-codes project
  (https://salsa.debian.org/iso-codes-team/iso-codes), LGPL 2.1 or later.
